sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Pass 3 Phase B primary assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848), Kunth (1869) & Chindapol et al. (2013) Scleractinian coral calice septal insertion, reduced 3D corallum & Keulegan-Carpenter surge morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 90.2/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 3 (v3) remediated evaluation of `2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py`. Both v2 remediation items are closed as honest reduced models: a kinematic 3D conical corallum (Wells 1956 apical-angle classes; septal insertion fronts N = 6 -> 12 -> 24 -> 48 stacked along z; dissepiments and synapticulae ablated at fixed outer geometry; apical angle 36.66 deg and septal thickness 0.277 mm measured from the pinned specimen), and a Keulegan-Carpenter oscillatory surge coupling of the Péclet boundary-layer flux (period-mean dipole <A_1> = 3e-16 vs unidirectional 0.647; quadrupole survives; KC_50 = 4.350 vs 2 pi ln 2 = 4.355). The Pass 2 content (hexameral doubling, Kunth Rugosa, Pe sweep, 7-species scaling, 40-septa specimen segmentation) is unchanged. 7 new Lean declarations (3 theorems + 3 lemmas, 0 sorrys), 12/12 self-test checks, 16 morphometrics, 5 rendered outputs. The score moves 91.6 -> ~90 because the re-audit penalises defects v2 passed: self-referential reference values, a closed-form-vs-itself Pe correlation, a phenomenological flux law with unsourced constants, a recalled cross-taxa table, and offline-recalled Pass 3 literature values with unverified DOIs. Overall 90.2/100 (faithfulness 89.6, reproducibility 91.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit e651a8b8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 89, Morphological realism / specimen match 91, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/coral_calice_septa_insertion_comparison.png: rendered output of 2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py at e651a8b8, image/png, 1001149 B, 2415×1551 px, artifact_sha256 cbee31b2b54319f1b348c2f440156314a4a9df33e06b7982c07b3a007457ba13 (sha256 cbee31b2b54319f1b348c2f440156314a4a9df33e06b7982c07b3a007457ba13), spec_fingerprint 0cff1aa51273708b6f3a81f44e78a537ce76e9aebe378d1738d5aa43189cae7d. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 0cff1aa51273708b6f3a81f44e78a537ce76e9aebe378d1738d5aa43189cae7d; artifact_sha256: cbee31b2b54319f1b348c2f440156314a4a9df33e06b7982c07b3a007457ba13; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/coral_calice_septa_insertion_reference.json=9984d41d12285bd0..., datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/corallum3d_surge_reference.json=5d3be9bdd005bfad..., datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/scleractinian_coral_septa_specimen.jpg=904035c936843361..., datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/scout_manifest.json=325761c7cb0d58db...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-coral-calice-septa-insertion-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848): hexameral cyclic septal insertion N_hex(k) = 6 * 2^(k-1) with decreasing radial reach of successive cycles | Kunth (1869): Paleozoic Rugosa serial insertion in four fossular loci, N_rugosa(m) = 6 + 4m | Chindapol et al. (2013): advection-diffusion limited accretive growth of Pocillopora verrucosa with upstream-polarised growth under unidirectional flow and symmetric, compact growth under bidirectional (surge) flow | Wells (1956) Treatise Part F: solitary corallum shape classes by apical angle (ceratoid, trochoid, turbinate, patellate) and the endothecal elements dissepiments and synapticulae | Keulegan & Carpenter (1958): the ratio U_max T / L governing oscillatory-flow forces on bodies; Falter et al. (2005) and Reidenbach et al. (2006): oscillatory flow enhances mass transfer to reef corals relative to unidirectional flow at the same speed; reconstructed_in_script: 2D calice insertion with perimeter-threshold triggering 2 pi R_k = N_hex(k) lambda_s, Kunth Rugosa comparison, a phenomenological boundary-layer flux law j(theta) = j0 (1 + beta sqrt(Pe) cos theta + gamma Pe/(1+Pe) cos 2theta) with Pe = 0 symmetry control, a reduced kinematic 3D conical corallum (cylindrical label volume) with stacked insertion fronts, pali, dissepiments and synapticulae ablated at fixed outer geometry, specimen-measured apical angle (side-profile cone fit) and septal thickness (0.80 R duty cycle), Otsu calice area fraction, an oscillatory surge quasi-steady closure with sgn(U) dipole and a renewal law eta(KC) = 1 - exp(-KC/2pi), KC sweep and reef KC estimates; transfer_boundary: The 3D corallum is kinematic (labels assigned from the cone profile), not accretive growth or mechanics; dissepiment/synapticula spacings and thicknesses are modelling choices tagged `provenance: model` | The quasi-steady surge closure gives <sqrt(Pe(t))>/sqrt(Pe_max) = 0.763 < 1, i.e. it cannot reproduce the oscillatory mass-transfer ENHANCEMENT of Falter 2005 / Reidenbach 2006; only the symmetry (dipole cancellation) claim of Chindapol 2013 is reproduced | The Law 3 flux law and the ellipticity formula are this script's ansatz, not equations from Chindapol et al. (2013); the JSON 'Eqs. (1)-(8)' pointer is unverified; does_not_claim: Finite-element or accretive growth of the corallum, validated dissepiment/synapticula geometry, a digitised cross-taxa septa table, verified Pass 3 DOIs, or that the 48 model rim septa match the specimen's 40." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py:148-160 and datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/pass3_citations.bib, corallum3d_surge_reference.json — the Pass 3 JSON and bib are not in `EXPECTED_SHA256`, and all Pass 3 DOIs (10.6028/jres.060.043, 10.4319/lo.2005.50.1.0246, 10.4319/lo.2006.51.2.1134, 10.1109/TSMC.1979.4310076) plus the carried BHL title-level Milne-Edwards DOI and the Kunth DOI are unverified offline. Pin the new files and verify every DOI online in the next round; flag `doi_verified_offline: true` only after resolution.",
            "remediation needed: 2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py:1808-1817, 1858-1867, 1888-1897 and datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/coral_calice_septa_insertion_reference.json (`reference_major/minor_septa_reach_ratio`) — the 7-species r reference (0.9985), the Pe-sweep r reference (0.9990) and the specimen reach-ratio reference (1.4368 = measured value) are hand-set or self-referential. Replace with literature-digitised anchors (e.g. a published Caryophyllia S1/S2 vs S3/S4 reach ratio, or Chindapol 2013 Fig. 5 asymmetry at matched Pe) or mark `derived_from: self` and exclude from the validation count.",
            "remediation needed: 2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py:2021 and :1090-1342 — `--seed` is a no-op; remove it or add a stochastic septal-insertion jitter so it has an effect. Panel titles in `render_comparison_figure` overlap horizontally at fontsize 9.6 and the 3D cutaway in the corallum3d figure is small; fix the layout.",
            "remediation needed: 2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py:435-501 and :246-365 — Law 3 is a phenomenological ansatz j0(1 + beta sqrt(Pe) cos theta + gamma Pe/(1+Pe) cos 2theta) with a 0.16 j0 wake floor (L454), the ellipticity formula (L462) and rim-modulation constants 0.035/0.025/0.42/0.35/0.06 (L274 ff.) that have no source; the JSON (L64) attributes it to Chindapol 'Eqs. (1)-(8)'. Either solve the 2D advection-diffusion boundary-layer problem numerically (Chindapol's actual model) or relabel the law as this script's reduced closure in the docstring, JSON and math-KG, and make the Pe = 36 ratio consistent (script 13.73 vs JSON 14.375).",
            "remediation needed: 2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py:504-580 — the quasi-steady surge closure gives <sqrt(Pe(t))>/sqrt(Pe_max) = 0.763 < 1, so it predicts LOWER mean transfer under surge than under a unidirectional current at the same speed, contrary to Falter et al. (2005) / Reidenbach et al. (2006). Add an unsteady boundary-layer renewal term (Stokes-layer thickness sqrt(2 nu/omega) or a Womersley-type correction) so the KC dependence of the MEAN flux, not only its symmetry, is tested, and replace the unvalidated eta(KC) = 1 - exp(-KC/2pi) with a fitted or derived law.",
            "remediation needed: 2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py:667-806 and datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/corallum3d_surge_reference.json:32-44 — the 3D corallum is a kinematic label volume: dissepiment spacing 0.60 mm, thickness 0.05 mm, tilt 0.5, synapticula radii {0.45, 0.65, 0.85} R and spacing 0.60 mm are `provenance: model`. Replace with digitised values from a longitudinal-section micrograph (e.g. a Flabellum or Fungia section vendored with SHA-256) and add a minimal accretion rule (e.g. dissepiment laid when the polyp base lifts by h_d) so the endotheca is grown, not placed.",
            "remediation needed: 2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py:873-930 and :1746-1755 — the specimen apical angle (36.66 deg) and costae count (15, undercounted) come from a side view with unknown pixel scale and oblique orientation; the septal thickness (0.277 mm) is calibrated on the same specimen it is compared to in the rim-area check (L1756-L1765). Vendor a second, independent Caryophyllia specimen (scaled side view and calice) so apical angle, costae and rim area are tested out-of-sample, and resolve the 48 model vs 40 specimen septa discrepancy by truncating S4 to the specimen's incomplete cycle.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/coral_calice_septa_insertion_reference.json:95-109 — the `cross_taxa_corallite_septa_table` (`observed_septa_mean`, `typical_peclet_Pe`, `major_minor_reach_ratio`) is recalled, not digitised; `evaluate_cross_taxa_corallite_scaling` (L933-L960) consumes it as if it were data. Replace with per-species values traced to Cairns & Kitahara (2012) generic diagnoses or Veron (2000) with page pins, or mark the table `provenance: recalled`.",
            "remediation needed: morphoeval/cloud/dispatches/slot-074.json (`slug: foraminifera-apertural-growth`) and the Pass 3 prompt (Ammonia beccarii / Topa & Tyszka 2002) do not describe this script; the pass3 telemetry `init` carries the foraminifera paper string. Correct the campaign slot metadata (or spin the foraminifera paper into its own slot) so later passes audit the right organism." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.902"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
}

